# The Gauges page's speed dial, Gspeed: an AGauge with airspeed and ground speed needles over a
# scale to its maximum, 60, placed as tabPage1_Resize places it for a page this size. A double
# click asks "Enter Max Speed", starting at 60 whatever the maximum is, and sets it: a number above
# the minimum changes it, anything else is refused as float.Parse refuses it. Galt, Gheading and
# Gvspeed are not ported.
# `GCSViews/FlightData.cs:3140-3148, 5217-5278, ExtLibs/Controls/AGauge.cs:446-462, 1499-1987`
#
# Needs SITL (a copter, standing still): tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/fly-gauges.gui -- tcp:127.0.0.1:5760

screen fly
window 1600x1200
budget 12

# The vehicle first: a click before its first heartbeat is a click the screen may forget
# (vehicle.connected only says the link is open).
expect vehicle.count > 0
click fly-tabs-right
click fly-tabs-right
click fly-tabs-right
click fly-tabs-right
click fly-tabs-right
expect fly.tabs.first 5
click fly-tab-gauges
expect fly.tab tabGauges
expect fly.page.overflow 0

expect fly.gauge.speed.max 60
expect fly.gauge.speed.size > 100
# Airspeed and ground speed, each held to the scale.
expect fly.gauge.speed.needles ~ ;

doubleclick fly-gauge-speed
expect fly.prompt Enter Max Speed
expect fly.prompt.value 60
key ctrl+u
type 25
click fly-prompt-ok
expect fly.prompt none
expect fly.gauge.speed.max 25

# Asked again it starts at 60; text that is not a number changes nothing.
doubleclick fly-gauge-speed
expect fly.prompt.value 60
key ctrl+u
type fast
click fly-prompt-ok
expect status Error: Input string was not in a correct format.
expect fly.gauge.speed.max 25
expect fly.page.overflow 0
